o keep schools open  that are  essentially in a way that can  stop them from transmitting the virus by  using very extensive testing in schools  just quickly would you consider  recalling parliament to vote on the  rules  well the rules are already in place uh i  was i got the question though  retrospective vote well there will be a  vote in parliament on these rules  yes uh in january but obviously having  taken the decision on  saturday lunchtime and brought it into  force  earl in the early hours of this morning  the we didn't have time to recall  parliament  from the point of decision at uh two  o'clock yesterday afternoon  when cabinet concluded uh in support of  these measures  before implementing in the early hours  of this morning  and therefore there will be a vote uh  after the fact when parliament comes  back in january  um we touched on vaccines a bit earlier  in the interview but it does feel like  it's worth asking again because it's  such a  something that all of us are clinging to  like there have been some concerns about  the speed  of the vaccine rollout though it was  said that we'll have to double the rate  at which we're rolling the fires of  acting out if you want to vaccinate all  vulnerable people  and key workers by easter a thing is  going to ramp up and how far  away are we from approving the oxford  vaccine  well um i feel i'm able to smile for the  first time  uh in uh several days the um uh the  the the are are accelerating and rising  fast the numbers that we're vaccinating  can you give us some new numbers then to  give us  well as of 8 o'clock yesterday morning  350 000 people have been vaccinated  uh we plan by the end of the weekend  to have something around the half a  million mark i'm not going to  put a that's not a target that's an  estimate um  and we're vaccinating more and more  people each day  we've now got over 400 different sites  that are vaccinating whereas at the  start of last week we only had 100 so  that's a multiple of four  so you can see that there is a  significant acceleration in the plans  some people have seen the total number  that have been vaccinated and  extrapolated that in a straight line  that's the wrong thing to do  because all the time every day we're  opening more and more vaccination  centers we're bringing more and more of  the gp led centers  on stream and how far away is the oxford  vaccine from approval  well that's a matter for the mhra the  regulator could it happen before  christmas  after christmas what's the uh it's very  tempting but i'm  just not going to speculate because i  respect their independence and that  includes  their independence to choose the timing  of any announcement  i need to ask you about brexit but just  very quickly if you knew  your neighbours for example breaking the  rules at christmas would you call the  police  well i just think it's so important that  every single person  follows these rules so would you call  the police well i think everybody should  follow the rules  and i don't think that's what i'm saying  it does but it but it needs saying  sophie because it's so important in this  in this  pandemic okay running out of time and i  do need to talk about brexit of course  just 11 days  until the end of the transition period  what state are the talks in how  confident are you that there'll be a  deal  well i i think the talks are continuing  um  i understand that the eu have put in a  deadline of having them concluded by  christmas  we want these talks to reach a positive  conclusion of course i want a deal  i think everybody wants a deal  unfortunately the eu have put in some  unreasonable demands  and i just you know obviously i've been  mostly concentrating on the pandemic but  i have been  looking at the detail of some of the  requests from the eu  they're unreasonable uh they they do not  respect the result of the referendum  what in particular is unreasonable well  over the uh the  sovereignty of our rules uh aro